**`PyObject_Malloc` is defined in `Objects/obmalloc.c`.**

On current CPython `main`, the public function is:

```c
void *
PyObject_Malloc(size_t size)
{
    /* see PyMem_RawMalloc() */
    if (size > (size_t)PY_SSIZE_T_MAX)
        return NULL;
    /* allocation stats... */
    return _PyObject.malloc(_PyObject.ctx, size);
}
```

It dispatches through the object-domain allocator (`_PyObject`), which is typically pymalloc (`_PyObject_Malloc`) or mimalloc (`_PyObject_MiMalloc`) depending on the build.

Relevant sources:

1. **Definition** — `Objects/obmalloc.c` (`PyObject_Malloc`, plus `PyObject_Calloc` / `PyObject_Realloc` / `PyObject_Free`) — [github.com/python/cpython blob main](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Objects/obmalloc.c)
2. **Same file, older layout (3.7)** — same function body without the later stats counters — [blob/3.7/Objects/obmalloc.c](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/3.7/Objects/obmalloc.c)
3. **Pymalloc backend** — static/internal `_PyObject_Malloc` in the same file, used when `WITH_PYMALLOC` is on — same `obmalloc.c`
4. **Declaration** — `PyAPI_FUNC(void *) PyObject_Malloc(size_t size);` in `Include/objimpl.h` — [objimpl.h](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Include/objimpl.h)
5. **Domain** — `PYMEM_DOMAIN_OBJ` covers `PyObject_Malloc` / `Realloc` / `Calloc` / `Free` — documented in `Doc/c-api/memory.rst` — [memory.rst](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Doc/c-api/memory.rst)
6. **Docs** — `PyObject_Malloc` documented as the object-allocator entry point (GIL / thread-state requirements vary by version) — same `memory.rst`
7. **Callers of the API** — e.g. `PyObject_New` is documented as allocating via `PyObject_Malloc` — `Doc/c-api/allocation.rst` — [allocation.rst](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Doc/c-api/allocation.rst)
8. **Header note** — comments in `Include/pymem.h` list `PyObject_Malloc` under the object domain (implementation still lives in `obmalloc.c`) — [pymem.h](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Include/pymem.h)
